{
  "_about": "Sanskrit <-> English <-> botanical lexicon for materia medica in the Charaka Samhita. 'sa' entries are case-SENSITIVE regexes over the NIIMH ITRANS-style romanization (A/I/U = long vowels, T/D/N/Sh = retroflex, sh = palatal, Ru = vocalic r, ~j = n-tilde, ~g = velar nasal). They match word stems as substrings because sandhi fuses words into compounds. 'en' entries are case-insensitive and anchored at a word start; they also carry common anglicized names (amla, giloy) so English queries and patents match. Ambiguous synonyms are deliberately left out (e.g. nAgara = ginger OR city, abhayA = haritaki OR 'fearless', tvak = cinnamon OR skin, kuShTha = Saussurea OR skin disease -> treated as the disease only).",
